# Checked against the references at random only (examples/asn1/choice.asn1).
#
# rasn 0.28, ALIGNED: Carry's ids, SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..3)) OF Small, it reads
# with its elements aligned (20.6: they are not), as alignment.vec's L.
deviates rasn Carry

# Found by byte mutation, derived by hand from X.691
# (02/2021). Pet ::= CHOICE {cat, dog, ..., fish Colour, bird}: after the
# extension bit, the index as a normally small number (23.8, 11.6), then the
# alternative as an open type (11.2).
#
# 1, then 1 (11.6.2's long form), padding, length 1, 00: index 0 = fish,
# which 11.6.1 puts in the short form (0 000000), then 01 00 (red).
reject! Pet c001000100  # asn1c, rasn, pycrate accept {"fish":"red"}
# 1, 1, padding, and a length of 0: the index in no octets. 11.7.4 wants a
# minimum octet encoding (11.3.6), unique: 0 in no octets would be a second
# encoding of 00.
reject! Pet c0000100  # asn1c, pycrate accept {"fish":"red"}; rasn rejects
# 1, 0 000000 (fish), and the open type's length in the two-octet form of
# 11.9.3.7, 80 01, for 1: 11.9.3.6 puts a length up to 127 in one octet.
reject! Pet 80800100  # asn1c, rasn, pycrate accept {"fish":"red"}
# Lone ::= CHOICE {only BOOLEAN, ...}: 1, 0 000000 (index 0), padding, 01 00:
# an alternative a newer version added (23.8), which ours keeps as its
# octets (OVERVIEW.md §1); JER has no form for it.
accept! Lone 800100 {"?unknown-extension":{"index":0,"octets":"00"}}  # asn1c, rasn reject a newer version's alternative; pycrate decodes it but cannot print it
